      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\n\n## Column Mapping\n- Chemistry department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- term: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- average number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- standard deviation of the number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- courses that have at least one associated course material: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n- maximum CIP program code: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE\n- departments that grant degrees: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- not the Mathematics department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- full department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Chemistry\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, give the department name and find the average and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, but only for the Chemistry department.\n```sql\nSELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS stddev_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IS NOT NULL GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME;\n```\n2. For each department, what is the maximum CIP program code among its courses, and what is the full department name, considering only departments that grant degrees, have a maximum CIP program code greater than 120000, and are not the Mathematics department (Course 18)?\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(scd.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE) AS MAX_CIP_PROGRAM_CODE, sd.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND scd.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE > 120000 GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME;\n```\n3. For the Chemistry department, give the department name, the average number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, the standard deviation of the number of enrolled students in those courses, the maximum CIP program code among its courses (considering only departments that grant degrees, have a maximum CIP program code greater than 120000, and are not the Mathematics department), and the full department name, in that order.\n```sql\nWITH Sub1 AS ( SELECT tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, AVG(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrolled_students, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS stddev_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON tso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID WHERE tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY IS NOT NULL GROUP BY tso.OFFER_DEPT_NAME ), Sub2 AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(scd.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE) AS MAX_CIP_PROGRAM_CODE, sd.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT sd JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = scd.DEPARTMENT WHERE sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND scd.CIP_PROGRAM_CODE > 120000 GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME ) SELECT s1.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s1.avg_enrolled_students, s1.stddev_enrolled_students, s2.MAX_CIP_PROGRAM_CODE, s2.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME FROM Sub1 s1 JOIN Sub2 s2 ON s1.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = s2.DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor the Chemistry department, for each term, provide the term, department name, the average number of enrolled students in courses that have at least one associated course material, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in those courses, the maximum CIP program code among its courses (considering only departments that grant degrees, have a maximum CIP program code greater than 120000, and are not the Mathematics department), and the full department name, in that order. Include subtotals for each term (the corresponding term field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all terms (the corresponding term field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the term if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by term and department. Do not return any rounded answers."
